meta {
  name: Verify - On-demand integrity check
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/profile-sections/verify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
  X-Company-ID: {{companyId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "employeeInternalID": "{{employeeInternalID}}",
    "profileSection": "PERSONAL",
    "recordIdentity": "",
    "currentValue": {
      "maritalStatus": "married",
      "address": "REDACTED-FOR-DOCS-EXAMPLE"
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("status is one of the documented verify outcomes", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect([
      "verified",
      "compromised",
      "deletion_verified",
      "no_anchor_found",
      "rejected",
      "error"
    ]).to.include(body.status);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /v1/profile-sections/verify

  On-demand integrity check (FR-10): recomputes the digest of a
  caller-supplied "current value" and compares it against the latest
  on-chain anchor for the same employee/section/record.

  Source: `integration-bridge/internal/pipeline/verify.go`.

  ## Request body
  | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `employeeInternalID` | string | yes | Same resolution as the history route. |
  | `profileSection` | string | yes | Must be one of the five ratified sections. |
  | `recordIdentity` | string | no | Multi-record domains only. |
  | `currentValue` | JSON object, or omitted/`null` | no | Omitted or explicit `null` asserts "this record is deleted" and short-circuits to `deletion_verified` — it is never treated as an attempted hash comparison against an absent value. |

  ## Response body
  | Field | Notes |
  |---|---|
  | `status` | See outcomes table below. |
  | `detail` | Present on non-terminal-success statuses. |

  ## Outcomes
  | status | Meaning | HTTP |
  |---|---|---|
  | `verified` | Recomputed digest matches the latest on-chain anchor. | 200 |
  | `compromised` | Recomputed digest does NOT match the latest anchor — the current value has diverged from what was anchored. | 200 |
  | `deletion_verified` | `currentValue` omitted/null — caller asserts deletion; no digest comparison performed. | 200 |
  | `no_anchor_found` | No anchor exists yet for this employee/section/recordIdentity. | 200 |
  | `rejected` | Malformed request or unknown `profileSection`. | 400 |
  | `error` | Auth failure, key/salt resolution failure, or ledger query failure. | 500 |

  A `compromised` result surfaces a real integrity finding — treat it the
  same as any tamper-evidence alert would be treated operationally
  (out of scope for this doc); do not silently retry it away.
}
